# What each account's sessions may do besides being themselves.
#
# A line is a name and its rights:
#   power    turn the machine off, and restart it
#   tasks    end any program, whoever's
#   become   run a command as another user with one's own password (`as`)
#   all      everything, the right to say who anybody is among it
#
# An account with no line has none of them, unless it is root, which has
# them all. `user NAME may RIGHT...` and `user NAME may not RIGHT...` write
# this file; `user` shows it. A right is handed to a session as it begins,
# so a change is there from the next login.
root all
